{"input": "What was the solution to risk appetite?", "answers": ["Dr David Blaney believed that governing bodies were not likely to exhibit as an imprudent risk appetite since they would see the potential risks coming through in forecasts, in requests for borrowings, predominantly and many other ways. Although the government body included a slightly different perspective, divisions were not falling short. Besides, commitments from enthusiastic people and occasionally with a slightly external perspective would also be a help."], "length": 10199, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The solution to risk appetite was to ensure that the governing bodies of Welsh universities are sufficiently rigorous and consistent in their approach to risk management. This was achieved by implementing a toolkit for governors, which provides information on the UK context and helps governors make informed decisions. The toolkit is intended to be refreshed and updated regularly to ensure that governors have the most up-to-date information available to them."}
