{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting began with a discussion on the TORRENT project completion being pushed for two years. Grad F then introduced intermediate categorization, which was his topic for his qualification exams. The team then discussed mean subtraction from SRI. Using it had led to an improvement in Meeting Recorder digits though near mic performance worsened. The professor points to pre-echoes as the culprit. The team continued to study differences between SRI and Aurora. The team thought it would be interesting to do the Aurora tests with the SRI system instead of the HTK. The team was also exploring the Wiener filter and VTS. The professor did not seem too excited about the VTS."], "length": 11881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discusses the current state of the project and the challenges faced. The team is close to being done with the project, but there are still some issues to be resolved. The team decides to wait for Sunil to arrive before doing his part of the project. They also discuss the possibility of combining the mean subtraction approach with the VAD approach. The team decides to test the SRI system trained on Macrophone data on the noisy TI-digits data. They also plan to test the Aurora system with the new front-end and acoustic models. The team discusses the possibility of using a different normalization approach for the VAD. They also discuss the possibility of using a combination of the different normalization approaches. The team decides to test the VAD on the TI-digits data and the Aurora system on the meeting digits data."}
